---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Fewer Photos"
  description="How Fewer Photos accesses your photo library, stores review progress and handles optional location postmarks."
>
  <article class="policy">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal information</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="effective-date">Effective from 19 August 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Overview</h2>

      <p>
        Fewer Photos is designed to work without an account. The application
        does not require your name, email address or profile information.
      </p>

      <p>
        Percival Studio does not receive copies of your photos or videos,
        review decisions or Stamp Book collection.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Photo library access</h2>

      <p>
        Fewer Photos requests permission to access your Apple Photos library so
        it can display photos and videos, organise them by month, update favourites
        and submit items you select for deletion.
      </p>

      <p>
        Access is controlled through iOS. You can change photo permissions at
        any time through the Settings application on your device.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Library review and deletion</h2>

      <p>
        Keep and delete decisions are stored by the application so that review
        progress can continue between sessions.
      </p>

      <p>
        Marking an item for deletion only adds it to the Fewer Photos
        Review Queue. The application does not request its removal from Apple
        Photos until you review the queue and explicitly confirm the deletion.
      </p>

      <p>
        iOS presents its own system permission prompt when Fewer Photos submits
        changes to the photo library.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Stamp Book progress</h2>

      <p>The application may store progress including:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Completed calendar months</li>
        <li>Total reviewed items</li>
        <li>Review activity dates and streaks</li>
        <li>Undo milestones</li>
        <li>Unlocked stamps</li>
        <li>Accepted and rejected location postmarks</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        This information is stored with the application on your device and is
        not sent to Percival Studio.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Location information in photographs</h2>

      <p>
        Some photographs contain geographic coordinates recorded by the camera
        or retained when the image was shared or downloaded.
      </p>

      <p>
        Fewer Photos may use those coordinates to offer optional town and
        country postmarks after enough associated photographs have been
        reviewed.
      </p>

      <p>
        To obtain a readable town and country name, the coordinate is submitted
        through Apple’s reverse-geocoding service. The photograph itself is not
        included in that request. Use of the Apple service is subject to
        Apple’s own privacy terms.
      </p>

      <p>
        Every town postmark requires your confirmation. Rejecting a suggested
        location removes those photographs from location-stamp progress without
        changing their Keep or Delete decisions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Accounts, analytics and advertising</h2>

      <p>
        Fewer Photos does not require an account and does not include
        third-party advertising, behavioural tracking or third-party analytics.
      </p>

      <p>
        Percival Studio does not sell personal information, photographs or
        review activity to advertisers or data brokers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The Fewer Photos website</h2>

      <p>
        This companion website provides product, privacy and support
        information. It does not connect to the Fewer Photos application or
        receive your photo library, review progress or Stamp Book collection.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Deleting application data</h2>

      <p>
        Removing Fewer Photos from your device removes its locally stored
        review and Stamp Book data, subject to any device backups managed
        through your Apple Account.
      </p>

      <p>
        Removing the application does not delete photos or videos from your Apple
        Photos library.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

      <p>
        This policy may be updated when the application’s features or data
        practices change. The effective date at the top of this page will be
        revised when an update is published.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>

      <p>
        For privacy or support enquiries, email
        <a href="mailto:support@thomaspercival.dev">support@thomaspercival.dev</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 49rem;
  }

  .page-header {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: auto;
    margin-bottom: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 7rem);
    padding: 0;
    display: block;
    border: 0;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--colour-accent-bright);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .effective-date {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  section {
    padding-block: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
  }

  section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  section p:last-child,
  section ul:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--colour-text-muted);
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }
</style>
